  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int_0^{1 / 2} f(x) d x < \\int_0^t f(x) d x < \\int_0^{3 / 4} f(x) d x$ Now, $\\int f(x) d x$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Y1rOmN-ABGVZnGrMYQXtd39YRuXI_W0Y9AEChDFAJoQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n=\\int\\left(1+2 x+3 x^2+4 x^3\\right) d x \\\\\n=x+x^2+x^3+x^4 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad \\int_0^{1 / 2} f(x) d x=\\frac{15}{16}>\\frac{3}{4} \\\\\n\\int_0^{3 / 4} f(x) d x=\\frac{530}{256} < 3\n\\end{gathered}\n$$",
